### Goal Model Decomposition

#### Goals Table

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Target Condition | Relation |
|------|------|---------|-----------|-------------------|----------|
| G1 | Manage the collection and delivery of resources efficiently | # | Achieve | Resources are collected and delivered to the specified location | - |
| G2 | Collect required resources from storage locations | ; | Achieve | All required resources are collected | AND |
| G3 | Deliver collected resources to the specified location | ; | Achieve | All resources are delivered to the specified location | AND |
| G2.1 | Select the optimal order to visit storage locations based on waiting time and path | - | Achieve | Optimal order is selected | AND |
| G2.2 | Request and retrieve resources from each storage location | - | Perform | Resources are retrieved from each storage location | AND |
| G3.1 | Transport resources to the specified location | - | Perform | Resources are delivered to the specified location | AND |
| G3.2 | Handle low battery during delivery phase | - | Perform | Resources are returned to a checkpoint and remaining task is assigned to another robot | AND |

#### Tasks Table

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots |
|------|------|----------|----------|-------------------|
| AT1 | Move to storage location to collect resources | AND | Storage Facility | [1,n] |
| AT2 | Deliver collected resources to the specified location | AND | Delivery Location | [1,n] |
| AT3 | Return resources to a checkpoint and assign remaining task | AND | Checkpoint | [2,n] |

### Summary of Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND][(#)]**
- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [AND][;]**
- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [AND][;]**
- **G2.1 -> AT1 [AND]**
- **G2.2 -> AT1 [AND]**
- **G3.1 -> AT2 [AND]**
- **G3.2 -> AT3 [AND]**

This decomposition ensures that the mission is executed efficiently, with parallel execution where possible, and fallback mechanisms to handle low battery situations.
